===Consonants===
{{Main|High German consonant shift}}
The main difference between Old High German and the [[West Germanic languages|West Germanic dialects]] from which it developed is that the former underwent the [[High German consonant shift|Second Sound Shift]]. The result of the sound change has been that the [[consonant]]al system of [[German language|German]] is different from all other West Germanic languages, including [[English language|English]] and [[Low German]]. The shift applied to different extents onto various dialects, added to other interdialectal variations, this makes a single "High German" system and precise articulations details thereabout difficult to reconstruct.

